# Acoustic Simulation Rules

## Geometry Source — Always Speckle

Room geometry is **never** a parametric box. It always comes from a live Speckle model fetched at
simulation time. The frontend user selects specific object IDs in the 3D viewer (or uses the whole
layer) and assigns materials per object in the UI before submitting the simulation.

### What the frontend sends

Both routers receive identical geometry inputs as `multipart/form-data`:

| Field | Type | Description |
| ----- | ---- | ----------- |
| `speckle_project_id` | str | Speckle project ID |
| `speckle_version_id` | str | Speckle version/commit ID |
| `layer_name` | str | Which Speckle layer to extract (default `"Acoustics"`) |
| `geometry_object_ids` | JSON str or null | Optional filter: object IDs selected in the viewer |
| `object_materials` | JSON str | `{"speckleObjectId": "materialId"}` per visible surface |
| `source_receiver_pairs` | JSON str | `[{source_id, source_position, receiver_id, receiver_position}]` — positions come from receiver objects placed in the Speckle 3D viewer |

